WEBVTT

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.760
<i>In the beginning, God created 
the heavens and the earth.</i>

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.890
<i>He followed them</i>

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.400
<i>with light, waters, and the land.</i>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.700
<i>Then he created the many animals
 that would inhabit it.</i>

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.990
<i>Or... that was the plan.</i>

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.010
<i>It got too tedious, so he outsourced it.</i>

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:36.180
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.280
This is Heaven's design team,

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.760
the department where animals are created.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.780
Shimoda-kun, as the newly-hired angel,

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.490
you'll be responsible for communication 
between the team and God.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.130
Yes, I will do my best!

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.400
Ueda-san, is that the new guy?

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.630
Yes, be nice to him.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.470
My name is Sh-Shimoda. It's nice to meet you!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.900
Yeah, yeah, welcome.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.570
So God doesn't create 
every single animal himself?

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:33.780
There are just too many, so he outsourced
 their design and creation to us.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:38.050
We're an OEM, manufacturing 
with the customer's branding.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.910
And God is our client.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.440
That's very illuminating!

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:46.140
It's time for the meeting. 
I hope you're ready.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:46.850
Yes!

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.350
Starting today, a new angel, 
Shimoda-kun, will be joining us.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.840
I'm so excited to be here!

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.640
Great.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.550
I'll jump right into the first agenda item.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.690
The order from the client 
we'll discuss today is:

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.710
"An animal that can eat leaves 
that are really high up."

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.280
There are three suggestions so far.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.360
We'll start with mine.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.200
Wow, a pegasus!

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.950
Indeed, a flying animal
 can reach leaves anywhere.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.030
Chief Tsuchiya, a horse again?

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.730
Is there a problem?

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.920
The horse design can be 
infinitely refactored.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.490
Chief Tsuchiya's best-known 
work is the horse.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.400
That's a masterpiece!

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.140
Yes, but because the horse
 is such a masterpiece,

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.230
he now bases all of his designs on it.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.310
Let's see the next 
suggestion, Mizushima-kun.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.120
Right.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.480
This is the Ping Pong Tree.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.730
I-Is this an animal?

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.540
Rather than eating leaves that are high up,

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.230
it looks more like a 
plant that gets eaten.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.190
I am not afraid of being innovative, 
and I endeavor to design

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.720
something that is not constrained 
by established norms.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.620
Yeah, I think you went too far.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.770
It can grow and shrink in length at will.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:05.270
And it captures prey with these balls.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.520
Ew, gross!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.890
Why would you design 
something like that?

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.210
It's not beautiful.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.640
Really? I like it.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.950
Yeah, Meido-chan has come up 
with carnivorous plants before.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.020
I can see why you like it.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.800
Carnivorous plants...

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.630
She's a designer, as well. Her
 best-known work is the poisonous frog.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.720
Now, on to the last suggestion.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.800
Unabara-kun came up with 
this long-necked deer.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.100
Well, if it's an animal that can
 eat leaves from the top of trees,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.290
I figured a long neck would help,
 so I tried that.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.050
<i>That's so simple.</i>

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.680
Such a simple idea, Unabara-kun.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.400
It is, huh?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.790
Anyway, let's toss it to the 
engineer to see if it could work

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:51.430
when we let it loose on Earth.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.230
Engineer?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:58.680
Designs must pass a number of tests 
so we're sure they'll survive on Earth,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.190
<b>Prototype Lab</b>

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.190
Hence this prototype lab.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.480
You submit the design proposals 
to the engineer here.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:10.200
The engineer makes prototypes based on 
our designs to see if they are viable.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.480
So there's even a mechanical department!

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.380
Oh, the door opened.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.590
That was rather quick.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.680
Tsuchiya-san...

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.600
I recall telling you that
 we cannot make a pegasus.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.860
Higuchi-san, I was hoping 
that you could do it anyway.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.860
I mean, it's cool. It's a horse.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.300
An animal this big cannot fly!

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.440
I've told you time and time again!

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.970
Please accept it already!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.490
That's Higuchi-san, our engineer.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:40.780
There's not enough muscle mass 
to use those wings to fly.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:44.230
That's right. Making an animal 
fly is a real challenge.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.030
Making it lighter wasn't easy, 
so I had to make the bones

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.180
and the feather stems hollow, dial up 
its excretion frequency, and so on.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:51.580
<b>Hollow Inside</b>

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.940
The pursuit of beauty isn't trivial.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.910
So, basically, making a 
pegasus reality means...

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:03.260
a mega-buff muscle horse that 
rapid-fires dung all over?

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:02.250
<b>Rat-tat-tat</b>

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.000
<b>Rat-tat-tat</b>

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>Rat-tat-tat</b>

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.540
That's why it's impossible.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.880
<b>Rejected</b>

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.870
Oh, no.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:12.260
And Mizushima-san, your 
Ping Pong Tree also won't work.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.170
It couldn't handle gravity.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.270
<b>Rejected</b>

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:19.660
Which leaves us with this long-necked deer.
 It won't work like this, though.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.870
Really? It should be able to eat...

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:26.140
I figured you'd say that, so I made 
it according to your original design.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.110
Cerebral anemia.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:41.010
If the neck is 10 meters long, 
you need a 1.5 ton heart

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:43.040
to transport the blood to the head.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.040
That's why it immediately 
collapses from lightheadedness.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.450
The poor thing!

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:50.140
Then how about making the 
legs longer instead?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:52.140
How will it drink water?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.170
That won't work.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.300
Then how about something in between?

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.370
Right.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.640
Then both leaves and 
water will be reachable!

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.560
It also relieves pressure on the heart 
and solves the lightheadedness.

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.580
All right, I'll take it back 
and make another prototype.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.660
But despite being this big, 
this pup only eats leaves, right?

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.370
I wonder if it can sustain itself.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:15.330
Then why not make it like the 
cows I made a while back?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:22.960
<b>Bacteria</b>

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:19.640
They keep bacteria in their gut 
that turns leaves into protein.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:22.960
With those, even a large 
animal can be an herbivore.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.190
Okay, I'll try that.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.710
I'll come, too. I want to taste it.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.950
As soon as he makes an animal, 
he does a taste test.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:34.090
A real diversity of ideas here, huh?

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.680
<b>And then...</b>

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.990
It's done.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.570
It's so big that it bonks its head.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:42.240
Should we add horns?

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.090
That's not a deer anymore.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.910
How about adding some horse elements 
to its face, something horsey?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.470
It already tastes good 
without horseradish.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.250
Stop horsing around.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.120
It's a bit sad without decoration.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.670
I'll come up with something!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.310
Oh, Shimoda-kun, did you just...

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.540
I got a message from God.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.110
God has spoken!

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.380
<b>Giraffe</b>

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.380
<b>Accepted</b>

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.370
Accepted!

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:13.120
Wow, it's the birth of a new life form!

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:15.760
Shimoda-kun, congratulations for 
finishing your first assignment!

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.010
I told you it's not getting enough protein.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.270
God has spoken again!

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.770
<b>Ping Pong
 Tree Sponge</b>

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.770
<b>Accepted</b>

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.620
Accepted!

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:27.560
Seriously?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:32.280
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.270
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.210
They're up to five meters tall.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:37.110
In the wild, they even sleep standing up.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.230
They give birth standing up, as well.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.880
The distance of their butt from 
the ground is about two meters.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.660
Wait, what about the babies then?

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.070
The moment they are born, they fall 
two meters and smack the ground!

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:48.160
That's terrible!

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.420
They have soft, tender bodies
so that they don't get hurt.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.450
This is how they drink water.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.570
Wouldn't the blood rush to their heads?

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.500
There's an organ near the brain that 
stores excess blood, so they're fine.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.700
They're really well tuned!

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.710
Among the tens of thousands 
of designs we create,

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:18.330
one will stand out and change everything.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.710
This is Tsuchiya-san's 
masterpiece, the horse.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.090
I wanted to add some 
revolutionary ideas to it.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.740
Front legs? Unnecessary.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.330
Hind legs? Unnecessary.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:35.080
There's no need to have a separate 
hole for intercourse and excretion.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:39.390
Thus, let me introduce this 
revolutionary animal to you.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:44.460
It's the snake.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.850
I hate this!

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.020
Why did our client allow this one to pass?!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.690
Obviously, because the snake's 
design is excellent.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.220
I'm so pissed!

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.930
I-Is something wrong?

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.380
That was an unexpected turn of events.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:02.100
Sometimes we are curious about how 
the animals we designed are doing,

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.240
so we take a peek at Earth.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.670
Indeed. The bird class that Kanamori 
did is designed really well.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.790
<b>Weaver
 Bird</b>

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.790
<b>Cry</b>

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.120
Especially their eggs.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.500
<b>Weaver
 Bird</b>

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.500
<b>Cry</b>

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.500
I love
 these
 eggs ♥

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.500
<b>Egg-Eating Snake</b>

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.230
What kind of snake only eats 
a certain bird's eggs?

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.260
A freaking gourmet?!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.920
It's fine! It means they're just that delicious.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.020
It's not fine!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.930
Incidentally, with its simple body shape,

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.260
the snake can move, climb, and capture prey.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:27.660
The more I hear, the more that 
thing sounds like it's cheating!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.990
I really want to see that snake suffer!

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.010
But how to do it...

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.280
How about an egg that's hard to eat?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.160
Good idea. Mizushima-san, 
you should help, too.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.190
How about adding spikes to the egg, then?

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.910
That would definitely hurt the 
mother when she's laying them!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.570
Then how about having the egg 
stick to the parent's belly?

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.580
Stick

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.270
The egg could walk.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.390
Or the parent could wrap it 
in a cloth and carry it.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.180
Something serious, please?

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.290
Then why not just make the shell so 
tough the snake can't digest it?

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.320
That's good! Right?

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.790
Let's have Higuchi-san make it.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:03.110
Here you go.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.170
Soon the chick will be born.

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.860
Oh no, it exhausted itself!

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:19.440
How about making it hatch faster 
when it senses a snake approaching?

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:20.830
Here you go.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:25.880
It hatched!

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:28.720
Of course.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.560
It's fine, it's just for the demo.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.970
Ask Higuchi-san to take it out.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:34.780
Okay.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.990
That's too bad. It was able to 
sense the snake's vibrations...

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.930
How about making it jump 
out of the nest to escape?

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.970
That's jumping from 
the frying pan into the fire.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.350
Yeah, they wouldn't be able to fly yet.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.840
The poor thing!

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:53.440
I guess that won't work unless they can 
fully move right after being born.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.730
Something like tadpoles.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:59.990
Oh, "new and fun frogs" are always welcome.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.400
All right, then I'll try submitting that idea.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:06.610
Well, basically, the snake has no weaknesses.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:12.450
By the way, the snake can smell by tasting 
particles in the air with its tongue.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:14.340
Th-That smug face again!

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.580
The snake and you both 
piss me off so much!

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:20.130
Just you wait! The birds won't 
be the helpless victims forever!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.630
<b>Days Later</b>

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.220
Kimura-san!

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.300
Your idea from the other day for the frog 
that can evade snakes got accepted!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.140
<b>Accepted</b>

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.140
<b>Red-Eyed
 Tree Frog</b>

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:29.300
Really?

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.610
Oh, so it passed.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.410
What kind of tweaks did 
you do? Please tell me!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.630
Well, as long as the snake 
is just looking at them,

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.740
the hatching won't begin.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.520
But as soon as the snake strikes,

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:45.670
the tadpoles sense the vibrations 
and escape into the water.

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:47.570
That's so clever!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:52.850
I'm jealous. My birdies 
still can't do anything.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.220
Kanamori-san...

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.800
Let's try thinking about it
 from the beginning.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.220
So, the snake is approaching.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.220
What happens next?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:06.440
It's hard. Even if they go higher, 
the snake will just climb after them.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:10.550
Freaking snakes... Freaking Mizushima!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.310
Couldn't the parent run away with the nest?

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.900
That's as ridiculous as the cloth 
carrier idea that Mizushima had.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.560
Oh, but wait.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.700
Wouldn't a nest like this 
make it harder to eat the eggs?

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:22.320
<b>Cross-Section</b>

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:24.490
If the nest is open on the bottom, 
the birdies can fly in,

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.380
but the snakes would fall down, right?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.580
I see! So let's come up with a 
bird that makes hanging nests!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.770
It can't be a new species! I want to 
get revenge on that gourmet snake!

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:36.910
So you'll do an update.

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:37.580
Yes.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:39.350
An update?

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.810
Oh, Shimoda-kun, you don't know yet.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:45.340
It means adding new features 
to existing creatures.

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.330
How about this design?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.100
<b>Accepted</b>

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:51.100
<b>Weaver Bird</b>

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:51.080
Update!

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.760
I'm so happy!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.280
Now they won't be easy prey for the snakes.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.520
<b>More Days Later...</b>

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:59.850
Good morning—

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:04.390
Wh-What happened to Kanamori-san?

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:08.120
No clue. She's been like that since 
she looked down at Earth.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:11.770
Apparently, the situation with 
the updated bird is escalating.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.330
The birds enhance their nests. 
The snakes redouble their attack intensity.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.990
Rinse, repeat.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:18.910
Want to look?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.420
<b>Type of Weaver Bird
</b>(Sociable Weaver)

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.420
It looks like a dungeon.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:26.970
It's not beautiful!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:31.190
And even though they're trying so hard,
 the snakes still keep coming.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:34.930
The birdies really do take 
after me! They're so brave.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.080
You mean insane?

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:41.820
That's why I thought of a new bird.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.520
Is it possible for me to present 
something to the client?

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.620
Uh, sure.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.450
The bird class is also always welcome.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:52.710
God has spoken!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.080
<b>Accepted</b>

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.080
<b>Secretary
 Bird</b>

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.090
Accepted!

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.600
Yay!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.190
How?!

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:00.590
This design has gone off the rails in regard
 to both personal resentment <i>and</i> taste!

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.580
Why did the client give this one a pass?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:09.090
Probably because my bird 
design is excellent.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:13.470
No, my adorable snake!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:17.980
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:17.060
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.990
Its red eyes make it so cute!
 Is it poisonous?

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:21.960
Nope.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:26.010
The purpose of these red eyes is to flash 
them at the enemies to startle them.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:29.300
And while the enemy is hesitating, 
they make their escape.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.480
They are seriously amazing at running away.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:34.870
I mean, they have the ability to escape 
even when they're in the egg!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:38.330
Besides snakes, they can also 
sense floods or droughts,

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.630
and turn into tadpoles early 
when they feel imminent danger.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:47.890
The red-eyed tree frog is a natural-born−
 No, a pre-birth master of danger mitigation!

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.780
Kimura-san, do you like frogs?

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:52.070
I do! I mean, they're tasty!

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.000
I kinda want to eat something tasty.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.640
Should we have a coffee break?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.000
I don't mean right now.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.910
Oh, then I'll make cream puffs
 for the next time.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:08.080
Shimoda-kun, you can make pastries?

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.720
No, what I meant is that 
I want to eat a tasty creature.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.650
All right! Let's make a tasty animal!

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:19.030
H-He's talking like he's about to cook...

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:21.520
There goes Kimura-kun's bad habit.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:26.200
Hey, Shimoda-kun and Unabara-san, 
what are you designing?

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.040
Can I do a taste test?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.880
N-Nothing's really done yet!

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:35.310
Oh, don't be like that. 
Let me see! I can help!

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.330
Does this always happen?

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:41.380
You know, you always treat me 
like I'm some weird freak,

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.210
but the Earth is built on the 
principle of the food chain.

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:46.430
Taste is very important!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.560
Its face is so slim!

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.420
What kind of creature is this?

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:56.260
Unabara-san is currently 
working on an order from God.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:58.580
It has to be an animal 
that eats tiny amounts.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.090
But nothing's settled yet. It's a rough draft!

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.920
Unabara-san, I finished 
that prototype you wanted.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.200
Want to go to Galapagos Island?

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.660
Galapagos Island?

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:11.530
It's an island for testing if prototypes
 will survive the conditions present on Earth.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:12.570
It's actually on Earth.

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.690
I've never been to Earth!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:15.710
I would love to go!

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.650
All right, let's all go have a barbecue!

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:25.230
<b>Testing Island
 Galapagos</b>

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.510
It's... plain.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.970
This is its default state.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:38.240
We run tests by applying themes with 
various conditions to the island.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:52.110
Wow, even the temperature 
and humidity changed.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.970
And this is what Unabara-san
 asked me to make.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.850
It's an animal that eats ants one by one.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:02.050
As requested, I made the tongue long 
so it can eat ants from ant hills.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.510
If you have any other requests, 
now's the time to ask.d

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.470
What is this pose?!

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.980
A threat! It's agonistic behavior!

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.190
I like it!

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.310
It eats ants, and it's not that fast.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:22.230
I think this one's yummy!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.830
You can tell just from that?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:30.010
In my experience, most animals that 
eat plants or insects are tasty.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:33.060
The less muscle mass they have, 
the tastier they are.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:35.870
Yes, I bet this one's delicious!

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.140
I... I see.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.420
That buff lion tasted super horrid.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.390
Most carnivores don't taste good.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.150
They're more tender if 
they have less muscle.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:50.410
The slow animals tend to melt in your mouth.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:52.760
It's because they have more 
unsaturated fatty acids.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.770
<b>Unsaturated Fatty Acids</b>

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:56.650
Speaking of, you know how a chicken's 
breast and thigh meat taste different?

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:00.910
<b>Breast</b>

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:00.910
<b>Thigh</b>

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.510
That's because they're 
different types of muscle.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:10.040
<b>Tires Quickly</b>

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:10.040
<b>Doesn't Tire Easily</b>

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:03.830
The chest muscles have
 explosive power and tire quickly,

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:06.660
while the thigh has endurance muscles 
that don't tire so easily.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.120
That means the breast meat
 ends up being drier.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:14.290
In other words, a marathon runner tastes 
better than a 100-meter sprinter.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.390
That analogy scares me!

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:25.510
Oh, that's the animal I came up with, 
the "lively sausage" (a working title).

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.990
It's literally a sausage, isn't it?

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:31.050
I did make it according to your request,

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:33.670
but it's got no eyes and no legs,
 and doesn't run away.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:36.180
If it's tasty, it's guaranteed to go extinct.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.440
Why not give it at least some mobility?

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:39.340
Sounds good!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.480
Hang on!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:45.190
The reason we from the design 
team do taste tests is to add

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:49.070
other abilities to make it easier 
for the tasty animals to survive!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.120
<b>Crap!
 I'm super delicious!</b>

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.250
<b>I'll hide in
 these thorns!</b>

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:53.190
And yet here you are, making animals 
that are just easy to eat.

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.200
Don't worry, Unabara-san.

00:19:55.990 --> 00:20:02.840
This sausage (working title) contains an 
alkaloid that many animals dislike.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.090
Yes, it's capsaicin!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.620
That's...

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.590
That's what makes chili peppers spicy.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.720
So it's just a spicy sausage!

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.180
So good!

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.340
When did you...

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.720
These spicy sausages are the best!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:19.310
Kimura-kun, capsaicin won't work on birds,

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:22.570
so you should probably 
add some other poison.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.490
Oh, I guess.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.980
Well, let's think about it while we eat.

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.480
Agreed!

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:32.720
The flavor is just being 
recreated from data.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.470
We should keep the food chain in mind, too.

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:39.250
Well, then Kimura-kun must 
undeniably be at the top of it.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.180
It's really good!

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:44.510
This is no good! It needs 
to have more defense...

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.030
Oh boy, you made major 
changes to the design.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.870
I'll have to remake it, then.

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.580
I'm sorry.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:56.950
But there's an animal that you 
could take notes from. Wanna see?

00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:59.260
I do! I want to sample it!

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:00.280
Hold on.

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:03.940
I wonder what it'll taste like.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:08.060
O-On Earth, I guess it's survival of the fittest...

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.880
Hey, the glyptodont is here.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.290
Kimura-san!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:25.800
God has spoken!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.800
<b>Anteater</b>

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.800
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.800
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.800
<b>Armadillo</b>

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.810
Accepted!

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:30.940
Wha? Right now?

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:36.060
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.050
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.530
It's so cute.

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:40.690
But it's got long claws, 
and it's not just cute.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.320
The anteater will go into its 
threat pose, so take a look.

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.070
So cute!

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.070
So it is just cute.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:52.400
The armadillo! It's a relative 
of the anteater, right?

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.940
The ones with the armor are the armadillos,

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:56.330
and the ones without are the anteaters.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:58.420
It's in such a nice ball shape.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.590
It's really strong this way! 
It can even reflect bullets.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:05.080
Amazing! And cute!

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:14.490
Oh, man... I saw Heaven.

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.570
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
